{"id":"9a2e9f4200af024a3d3b8a2ef8ab1243c26ab8e4","axis":"silent","repo":"mongodb/mongo","sha":"9a2e9f4200af024a3d3b8a2ef8ab1243c26ab8e4","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".bazelrc","lines":["@@ -552,10 +552,18 @@ common:macos --//bazel/config:compress_debug_compile=False"," common:windows --//bazel/config:linkstatic=True"," common:windows --//bazel/config:skip_archive=False"," ","-# The only Windows compiler we support is MSVC.","+# Native Windows builds use MSVC; the default cross route uses clang-cl with","+# the pinned MSVC ABI and SDK inputs."," common:windows --//bazel/config:compiler_type=msvc"," common:windows --//bazel/config:linker=auto"," ","+# Explicit opt-in to fully native MSVC. --config=local controls execution only:","+# it keeps the cross toolchain and runs Linux build actions in a local container.","+common:windows-native --config=no-remote-exec","+common:windows-native --platforms=@internal_platforms_do_not_use//host","+common:windows-native --repo_env=BAZEL_DO_NOT_DETECT_CPP_TOOLCHAIN=0","+common:windows-native --enable_platform_specific_config","+"," # Data dependencies don't work in bazel run or bazel test on windows without this"," startup --windows_enable_symlinks"," common:windows --enable_runfiles","@@ -566,9 +574,8 @@ test:windows --test_env=MONGO_BAZEL_BASH"," test:windows-cross-x86_64 --run_under=//bazel:windows_test_launcher"," test:windows-cross-x86_64 --test_env=MONGO_BAZEL_BASH"," ","-# Static linking and the native launcher for Evergreen Windows unit-test tasks.","+# Static linking and the host launcher for Evergreen Windows unit-test tasks."," common:windows_unittest --linkstatic=True","-common:windows_unittest --config=remote_link"," test:windows_unittest --run_under=//bazel:windows_test_launcher"," build:windows --action_env=MSYS=winsymlinks:nativestrict"," test:windows --action_env=MSYS=winsymlinks:nativestrict"],"additions":10,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"bazel/docs/windows_hermetic_container_cross.md","lines":["@@ -2,8 +2,9 @@"," "," This mode is for Windows hosts that want Bazel to produce Windows x86_64 artifacts with the hermetic"," Windows cross toolchain. Bazel runs on the Windows host, C++ and generated-source actions run on","-Linux RBE through the cross toolchain wrapper entry points, and `bazel run` for test targets","-executes the resulting Windows binary from the local workspace.","+Linux RBE through the cross toolchain wrapper entry points, and link/package actions use a local","+Linux container. `bazel test` and `bazel run` for test targets execute the resulting Windows","+binaries on the host through the Windows launcher."," "," ## Usage"," ","@@ -14,25 +15,38 @@ bazel build install-dist-test"," .\\bazel-bin\\install-dist-test\\bin\\mongod.exe --version"," ```"," ","-Windows builds use the original native MSVC toolchain by default. To opt into the experimental","-host-cross integration, pass `--config=windows-cross-x86_64` explicitly:","+Windows `build`, `test`, `fetch`, `cquery`, and `aquery` commands default to","+`--config=windows-cross-x86_64`. The host needs the pinned MSVC/SDK inputs and a Linux container","+engine, described below. Explicit `--platforms` choices are preserved, including choices from","+imported RC files and automatic `:windows` config sections. `--config=local` keeps the cross","+toolchain and executes Linux build actions in a local container, without remote execution, cache, or","+credentials. Community checkouts use this local cross path by default. `--config=no-remote-exec`","+also uses local container actions while retaining remote cache access. On other host operating","+systems, select the cross configuration explicitly:"," "," ```powershell"," bazel build --config=windows-cross-x86_64 install-dist-test"," ```"," ","-To make build-oriented commands such as `build`, `fetch`, `cquery`, and `aquery` default to cross","-mode for the current shell, set:","+Fully native MSVC requires an explicit opt-in:"," "," ```powershell","-$env:MONGO_WINDOWS_CROSS_DEFAULT_CONFIG=\"1\"","+bazel build --config=windows-native install-dist-test"," ```"," ","-With that opt-in, `bazel run` also defaults to Windows cross mode for test targets, builds them","-through the cross wrapper/RBE path, and runs the produced `.exe` on the Windows host:","+This config selects the host toolchain and disables remote execution. It cannot be combined with","+`--config=windows-cross-x86_64`. The existing shell-wide native rollback remains available:","+","+```powershell","+$env:MONGO_WINDOWS_CROSS_DEFAULT_CONFIG=\"0\"","+```","+","+By default, `bazel run` also builds test targets through the cross wrapper/RBE path and runs the","+produced `.exe` on the Windows host:"," "," ```powershell"," bazel run +stdx_test","+bazel test +stdx_test"," ```"," "," To bypass the host-cross integration even when the config is explicit:","@@ -41,8 +55,34 @@ To bypass the host-cross integration even when the config is explicit:"," $env:MONGO_BAZEL_USE_HERMETIC_CONTAINER=\"0\""," ```"," ","-`bazel test` is not auto-routed through Windows cross mode. For non-test `bazel run` targets, build","-the target and run the downloaded `.exe` from PowerShell.","+For non-test `bazel run` targets, build the target and run the downloaded `.exe` from PowerShell.","+","+## Tests and debug symbols","+","+`--config=windows_unittest` selects static linking and the Windows test launcher. The Windows cross","+wrapper adds remote linking when remote execution is enabled. With `--config=local` or","+`--config=no-remote-exec`, compilation and linking use the local Linux container. Windows tests run","+locally in both modes. Native MSVC opt-in retains native linking. The cross configuration omits PDBs","+from its automatic download regex. Evergreen's optimized unit-test tasks use","+`--remote_download_outputs=minimal`; failed-test gathering downloads PDB/debug files while retaining","+the original build configuration. Debug variants retain their normal symbol settings.","+`--debug_symbols=False` suppresses compiler and linker symbols, including native MSVC `dbg` and","+`fastbuild` modes.","+","+Evergreen compile and unit-test tasks use `windows-2022-wsl2-xxlarge`, which supplies the local","+Linux action container. Runtime-only resmoke tasks retain their smaller Windows distros. Release","+packaging also uses the cross toolchain: published release builds execute compile/link actions","+locally in the Linux container under `public-release-local`, with the release cache restrictions","+preserved. No Evergreen task opts into native MSVC. Packaging requires a container-capable","+`release-*` host to satisfy the release guard; without a Linux container engine, the build fails","+instead of falling back to MSVC. The shared shell helper enables cross RBE before generating the","+Evergreen RC. The native switches above are for manual diagnosis only.","+","+Rust uses a Linux-hosted toolchain targeting `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` (the Windows ABI, not the MSVC","+compiler). Cargo build scripts and their Rust compiler helpers execute on Linux, and C/C++","+dependencies use the cross Clang toolchain. These actions run in the local container for local and","+release builds, or on Linux RBE otherwise. Wasmtime's downloaded Windows CLI remains a host-local","+tool for AOT generation."," "," ## Replaying compilation database commands"," ","@@ -167,6 +207,13 @@ digest."," "," ## WSL2 Docker Engine"," ","+Evergreen uses WSL hosts for compilation, Bazel unit tests that compile their binaries, and","+compile-command replay. Resmoke suites and benchmarks that consume archived binaries use their","+original Windows test distros, including expandedports images for connection-heavy suites. Keep","+their `large_distro_name` and task distro assignments intact when overriding release build hosts for","+patch testing. `requires_compile_variant` identifies an artifact dependency; it does not by itself","+mean that a task compiles code.","+"," Windows cross builds need Linux containers. Docker Desktop may work on desktop Windows, but Windows"," Server native Docker/Mirantis runtimes only run Windows containers and cannot run the Linux RBE"," image used by the cross action wrappers."],"additions":58,"deletions":11,"truncated":false},{"path":"bazel/wrapper_hook/BUILD.bazel","lines":["@@ -200,6 +200,7 @@ py_test(","         \"hermetic_container/cross/windows_test.py\",","     ],","     data = [","+        \"//:.bazelrc\",","         \"//bazel:hermetic_container/hermetic_container.py\",","         \"//bazel/platforms:remote_execution_containers.bzl\",","         \"//bazel/toolchains/cc/mongo_apple_cross:macos_cross_action_wrapper.py\","],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"bazel/wrapper_hook/hermetic_container/cross/windows.py","lines":["@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@","     _bazel_effective_options,","     _bazel_output_base,","     _config_requested,","+    _remote_execution_disabled_for_options,","     _remote_link_requested,","     _replace_bazel_startup_option,","     _repo_env_overrides_from_args,","@@ -55,6 +56,7 @@","     _bazel_command,","     _bazel_command_index,","     _bazel_run_target,","+    _config_values,","     _env_is_false,","     _env_is_true,","     _info,","@@ -78,9 +80,18 @@","     _label_to_host_executable,","     _macos_cross_linux_python_options,"," )","-from .macos import _macos_cross_remote_execution_disabled"," "," WINDOWS_CROSS_CONFIG = \"windows-cross-x86_64\"","+WINDOWS_NATIVE_CONFIG = \"windows-native\"","+","+# Cross defaults replace these native repository defaults. User platform choices","+# still opt out; user executor settings choose local container execution or RBE.","+WINDOWS_NATIVE_DEFAULT_RC_OPTIONS = frozenset(","+    {","+        (\"build\", \"--platforms=@internal_platforms_do_not_use//host\"),","+        (\"common:windows\", \"--remote_executor=\"),","+    }","+)"," "," "," WINDOWS_CROSS_DEFAULT_CONFIG_ENV = \"MONGO_WINDOWS_CROSS_DEFAULT_CONFIG\"","@@ -111,6 +122,7 @@","         \"build\",","         \"cquery\",","         \"fetch\",","+        \"test\",","     ]"," )"," ","@@ -121,6 +133,43 @@"," WINDOWS_CONTAINER_ACTIONS_LAYOUT_VERSION = \"v1\""," WINDOWS_CROSS_UNIX_ROOT = \"C:/bazel-linux\""," WINDOWS_LOCAL_CONTAINER_MNEMONICS = (\"CppLink\", \"PackageZip\")","+# Actions using tools built for the Linux execution platform cannot run on the","+# Windows client. In local mode they all use the same persistent container.","+WINDOWS_CROSS_CONTAINER_MNEMONICS = (","+    *WINDOWS_LOCAL_CONTAINER_MNEMONICS,","+    \"CppCompile\",","+    \"CppArchive\",","+    \"ConfigHeaderGen\",","+    \"TemplateRenderer\",","+    \"IdlcGenerator\",","+    \"Genrule\",","+    \"Rustc\",","+    \"RustcMetadata\",","+    \"CargoBuildScriptRun\",","+    \"CargoBuildScriptCopy\",","+    \"WindowsRC\",","+    \"WasmAotCompile\",","+)","+WINDOWS_HOST_LOCAL_MNEMONICS = (","+    # These rules constrain their interpreter and dependencies to the native","+    # Windows host. They must bypass both Linux RBE and the persistent container.","+    \"CertificateGenerator\",","+    \"ExtractCertificateGenerationYear\",","+    \"MongoPrettyPrinterTestCreation\",","+    \"EmbedPublicKeyHeader\",","+    \"GpgExportArmored\",","+    \"GpgSign\",","+    \"MongoInstallRule\",","+    \"SolibSymlink\",","+    \"ExtractDebugInfo\",","+    \"StripDebugInfo\",","+    \"CcGenerateIntermediateDwp\",","+    \"CcGenerateDwp\",","+    \"DefParser\",","+    \"WixCandle\",","+    \"WixLight\",","+    \"MsiTrim\",","+)"," WINDOWS_CONTAINER_PREFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 900"," WINDOWS_CONTAINER_RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT_KEYS = (","     \"APPDATA\",","@@ -197,36 +246,67 @@ def _bazelrc_windows_repo_envs(repo_root: pathlib.Path) -> dict[str, str]:","     return values"," "," ","+def _windows_cross_user_options(","+    args: Sequence[str],","+    env: Mapping[str, str],","+    repo_root: pathlib.Path,","+    *,","+    platform_specific_only: bool = False,","+) -> list[str]:","+    return _bazel_effective_options(","+    